WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.216
( music)

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.642
- OK, thank you.

00:00:08.642 --> 00:00:12.870
I teach a course, Biology
101, and last Fall

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.130
it enrolled 220 students.

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.210
This big group of people here is as large

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.830
as many classes at Yale College,

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.060
these are just the
instructors for the course,

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.641
it's two professors
and 12 teaching fellows

00:00:23.641 --> 00:00:26.360
and together we are grading and

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.960
providing feedback on 3,000 assignments

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.850
that the students hand
in during this course.

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:34.990
And this is logistically
daunting and we use Canvas

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:38.300
as our organizing tool
to get us through this.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.640
One of the simplest things
that we use Canvas for

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.530
is to just distribute course
materials to the students.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.138
So here in this Files
function, we've loaded up

00:00:46.138 --> 00:00:49.130
a whole bunch of folders of materials,

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.070
so lecture notes for every lecture,

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:52.580
a study guide for every lecture,

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.300
all of the reading assignments.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.500
Students just go in
here, download everything

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.560
electronically, there's
180 megabytes of materials

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.620
that students can
download in these folders.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.290
I want to focus on our
homework assignments.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.540
So students go into the Assignments tool,

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.210
they pull up a homework assignment,

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.676
they get information on it including

00:01:10.676 --> 00:01:13.670
when it's due, the date and the time.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:16.120
They click on this link,
they download the assignment

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.880
as an electronic document
and then they fill in

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.220
their answers to the
questions electronically.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:25.110
They go to this screen,
they select the file

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:26.912
on their computer, they submit it

00:01:26.912 --> 00:01:30.360
and that uploads the completed assignment.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.890
And then our very favorite
feature for this class of Canvas

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:37.270
is SpeedGrader, which
was mentioned earlier.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:38.910
So the teaching fellow goes in,

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.150
just gets a list of the
students in their section

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.650
whose work they're
grading, they don't need to

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.010
download the files for those assignments.

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:48.620
They just click on the
student and we get this

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.050
Preview window, which shows the contents

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:52.940
of that homework assignment.

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:56.640
And now, using these
tools, the teaching fellow

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.070
can go in and start
marking up the assignment,

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:01.720
they can write you got five
points on question one.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.590
Here the student wrote something
that wasn't quite right,

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.580
the teaching fellow makes a note here

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:08.630
telling the student something.

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:12.194
At the end they can say
great work on this assignment

00:02:12.194 --> 00:02:14.850
and then they fill in a score here

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:17.920
and that automatically goes
into the Grades function,

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:19.700
they click submit and they're done.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.250
And I just want to emphasize
we never downloaded anything,

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:24.700
we never uploaded
anything and when you have

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:28.763
213 assignments to go through,
that's a huge time saving.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.590
Those scores that we enter
automatically go into

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:34.320
the Grades function, which creates

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.750
this ginormous spreadsheet.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:38.690
And I know you can't read the details,

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:40.650
but just to point out how this works,

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:44.870
every row is a student,
every column is an assignment

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:48.130
and then we've got a final
score here at the end.

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:50.820
And so here we're viewing all
the students in the course,

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.240
but a teaching fellow
could just pull up records

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:55.510
for the students in their section.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:56.970
When we set this up at the beginning

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.200
of the semester, we assigned a point value

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.378
or a percentage value
for every assignment.

00:03:02.378 --> 00:03:06.840
And then this system can
automatically take those values

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:09.750
into account and calculate a final score.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:12.810
And we use a complex grading
scheme in this course,

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:16.120
so, for example, there are
five homework assignments

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:18.190
and the students are
allowed to drop the score

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:21.400
for their lowest scored
homework assignment.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.257
And perhaps you can see here
in these first five columns,

00:03:24.257 --> 00:03:27.270
for every student one of
the scores is grayed out,

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:29.061
and that's the one that
Canvas automatically

00:03:29.061 --> 00:03:31.030
determined was the lowest score and

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:33.753
it got dropped from the final calculation.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:38.569
We can see here the scores for
every student in the class.

00:03:38.569 --> 00:03:40.828
The students, the
individual students can see

00:03:40.828 --> 00:03:43.210
their own scores that we've entered.

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:45.301
And there's another function that we love,

00:03:45.301 --> 00:03:48.170
so here's a detail from
the Grades feature.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:52.430
We pull up specific
details about an assignment

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:54.920
and while we're entering
the scores and proofreading

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:56.672
and making sure we did
everything accurately

00:03:56.672 --> 00:03:59.210
we mute the assignment,
so the students can't see

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:02.010
when we by mistake we
entered an incorrect score.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:03.830
When we've determined that we've entered

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:07.340
everything correctly, we can
go in and unmute the assignment

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:09.900
and now, for the final
exam, all of the grades

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.230
are released to the
students at the same time.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.683
When we have 3,000 scores
that we have to enter

00:04:14.683 --> 00:04:16.890
we want to make sure we
don't make a mistake,

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:19.010
and because the students
can see their own scores

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:21.883
they make sure that we've
entered everything correctly.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:25.560
We often communicate with
our students by e mail

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:27.816
and Canvas automatically interfaces

00:04:27.816 --> 00:04:29.960
with the Registrar's computer.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:31.689
So it makes these e mail lists,

00:04:31.689 --> 00:04:34.680
here one for every student in the course,

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.010
so we can blast an email to everybody,

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.920
but also automatically
set up are e mail lists

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:42.340
for each one of the 13 sections,

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.110
discussion sections in the course.

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:45.861
So the teaching fellow leading a section

00:04:45.861 --> 00:04:48.550
can click on one of those and communicate

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.550
just with the students in their section.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.330
There's a new tool that
was beta tested this year

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:56.210
that we use called Sign Up that we use

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:59.340
to set up office hours
and we like that tool.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:02.039
So here we are, I decide that I've got

00:05:02.039 --> 00:05:03.990
three hours available tomorrow

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:05.670
when I could meet with students.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:09.255
I go into Sign Up, I tell it
I'm available from 12 to three.

00:05:09.255 --> 00:05:12.340
I decide that I'm going
to set up half hour

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:14.350
time slots so it divides it there.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:15.670
I decide that I'm willing to see

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:18.380
one student at a time, so I set that up.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.811
Now we have a little menu, I say OK.

00:05:20.811 --> 00:05:23.980
Canvas automatically e
mails all the students

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:26.090
in the course and says
hey, Professor Koelle's

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.790
available from 12 to three tomorrow

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:29.430
and there's some new slots available.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:31.030
They go in here, click on one of those,

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.900
that sets up an appointment.

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:35.785
There's then an itinerary
that I can see on Canvas

00:05:35.785 --> 00:05:39.020
of all the students who are
coming at specific times

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.929
and they show up in my office.

00:05:40.929 --> 00:05:42.900
We also use this to set up lunches,

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.680
I have lunch with a group of five students

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:46.920
at a time every Wednesday after lecture.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:49.030
You can set up a slot here that lets

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:50.719
five students sign up for that time

00:05:50.719 --> 00:05:52.973
and it takes care of all the logistics.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:55.863
Large courses, they can be impersonal,

00:05:55.863 --> 00:05:58.510
you'd like to be able to have one on one

00:05:58.510 --> 00:05:59.840
interactions with the students

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:02.190
and this really facilitates that.

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:04.603
OK, thank you and I'll take questions.

00:06:04.603 --> 00:06:06.853
(applause)

00:06:12.513 --> 00:06:13.550
- [Audience Member] In the Sign Up section

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:16.320
are those slots blinded so
other students couldn't see?

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.000
- I believe so, so the student just sees

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.783
that a slot is available.

00:06:19.783 --> 00:06:21.940
I can see who's coming, but they

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:24.150
can't see the other students.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:24.983
- [Audience Member] You can choose that

00:06:24.983 --> 00:06:26.470
as an option, though, if you wanted to

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:28.114
allow students to swap
spots, you have the choice

00:06:28.114 --> 00:06:30.364
to determine whether or
not they will see it.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:36.560
- [Audience Member] I have a question for,

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:40.202
not for you for the
technician, cause we used to

00:06:40.202 --> 00:06:44.310
grade students homework, I, on Canvas,

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:46.967
but because he's reading Chinese,

00:06:46.967 --> 00:06:50.020
so now for some reason this semester

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:51.880
we cannot see their responses, it's all

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:54.793
just boxes instead of caricatures.

00:06:55.959 --> 00:06:58.618
Yeah, last year it worked
well, but this year

00:06:58.618 --> 00:07:02.270
we cannot just grade it on Canvas

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:05.063
and we have to download
it and then upload, so.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:08.307
- That sounds like a bug.

00:07:08.307 --> 00:07:09.780
(laughs)

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:12.650
Send us an e mail at
Canvas@Yale and we can work with

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:16.210
because we have contacts at Instructure,

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:17.693
which is the company that created Canvas

00:07:17.693 --> 00:07:19.320
and we can work with them to find out

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:20.360
why these things are going wrong.

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:22.370
So the more people who give us examples

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:23.550
of courses where this is failing,

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:25.460
the more they will have, you know,

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:27.210
something to dig into and research

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:29.460
to find out why this is
happening and fix it.

00:07:34.964 --> 00:07:36.631
Any other questions?

00:07:40.389 --> 00:07:41.222
All right.

00:07:41.222 --> 00:07:43.472
(applause)

00:07:45.357 --> 00:07:47.940
( music)

